    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Sardinia, New York was founded in 1821 when settlers split from the town of Concord.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sardinia%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By 1823 the town already boasted farms, churches, a post office, taverns, a carding mill, a woolen factory, a gristmill and a tannery.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sardinia%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The hamlet of Chaffee sprang up in the mid‑1800s after the Springville and Sardinia Railroad cut through the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sardinia%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Sardinia’s historic heart houses the Old Sardinia Town Hall, now the Sardinia Historical Society museum, listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sardinia%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Founded in 1968, the Sardinia Historical Society is run entirely by volunteers who preserve the town’s heritage and host yearly events.",
